cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this replication or its derived evaluation splits, please cite this
  artifact and, separately, the original paper it replicates and the Chronos-2
  checkpoint it evaluates.
title: >-
  Do frozen time-series foundation model embeddings help RUL prediction, and are
  the resulting uncertainties honest? A public-data replication with a
  calibration extension
abstract: >-
  A replication of "Time-Series Foundation Model Embeddings for Remaining Useful
  Life Estimation" (arXiv:2606.11990) on the public NASA C-MAPSS FD001 benchmark,
  extended with a calibration analysis the original does not report: coverage,
  sharpness, regime-conditioned coverage, and split-conformal repair. Includes
  attribution controls bounding what the frozen pretrained representation can be
  credited with.
